DrorPay uses Socket.IO to provide bidirectional, real-time communication between clients and servers. The implementation is designed with two separate socket systems to avoid conflicts and ensure reliability:  
#### Payment Socket Manager
The Payment Socket Manager handles all real-time communication related to payment gateway functionality. It's completely separate from the Twilio socket system to prevent any interference.  
**Key Features:**
- **Room-based Communication**: Each payment gets its own room for isolated updates
- **Order-based Rooms**: Uses platform order IDs so platforms can join before creating payment intents
- **Event Broadcasting**: Sends targeted updates only to relevant platforms
- **Connection Management**: Handles client connections, disconnections, and errors
- **Security**: Validates platform permissions before allowing room access
```javascript
// src/utils/paymentSocket.js
class PaymentSocketManager {
constructor() {
this.io = null;
}

setupPaymentSocket(io) {
this.setSocketIO(io);

io.on("connection", (socket) => {
console.log("Payment client connected:", socket.id);

// Join payment room using order ID or transaction ID
socket.on("join-payment-room", async (data) => {
const { platform_order_id, platform_id, platform_transaction_id } = data;

// Validate and join room
const roomName = `payment-order-${platform_order_id}`;
socket.join(roomName);

// Send confirmation
socket.emit("payment-room-joined", {
platform_order_id,
message: "Ready to receive payment updates"
});
});

// Handle disconnect
socket.on("disconnect", () => {
console.log("Payment client disconnected:", socket.id);
});
});
}

// Emit payment events to room
emitPaymentStatusUpdate(platform_transaction_id, statusData) {
const roomName = `payment-order-${statusData.platform_order_id}`;
this.io.to(roomName).emit("payment-status-update", {
platform_transaction_id,
...statusData,
timestamp: new Date()
});
}
}
```  
#### Twilio Socket Integration
The Twilio Socket Integration manages DrorPay's customer support call center. This system allows admin agents to handle customer support calls in real-time with features like call routing, queue management, and agent status tracking.  
**Call Center Features:**
- **Intelligent Call Routing**: Calls are routed to appropriate agents based on language and expertise
- **Queue Management**: Calls are queued when all agents are busy
- **Agent Management**: Real-time agent status tracking (available, busy, away)
- **Multi-language Support**: Automatic language detection and routing
- **Call Recording**: All calls are recorded for quality assurance
- **Real-time Dashboard**: Admins can see live call status and agent availability
```javascript
// src/utils/socket.js - Existing Twilio integration
const setupTwilioSocket = (io) => {
io.on("connection", (socket) => {
console.log("Admin connected:", socket.id);

// Handle admin joining for call management
socket.on("join-admin-room", async (data) => {
const { agentId, roleSlug } = data;
await twilioService.registerAgent(agentId, roleSlug);
socket.join("admin-room");

// Send current call status
const activeCalls = twilioService.getActiveCalls();
socket.emit("active-calls-update", { activeCalls });
});

// Handle call actions
socket.on("pickup-call", async ({ callSid, agentId }) => {
await twilioService.dequeueCall(callSid, agentId);
});
});
};
```

DrorPay uses a multi-layered authentication system that provides different levels of access for different types of users while maintaining security and usability.  
#### JWT Token Management
```javascript
// Token generation
const generateToken = (user) => {
return jwt.sign(
{
id: user.id,
email: user.email,
role: user.role
},
process.env.JWT_SECRET,
{ expiresIn: '7d' }
);
};

// Token verification middleware
const auth = async (req, res, next) => {
try {
const token = req.header('Authorization')?.replace('Bearer ', '');

if (!token) {
return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Access denied' });
}

const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
const user = await User.findById(decoded.id);

if (!user) {
return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
}

req.user = user;
next();
} catch (error) {
res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
}
};
```  
#### Role-Based Access Control
```javascript
// Admin authentication
const adminAuth = async (req, res, next) => {
try {
const token = req.header('Authorization')?.replace('Bearer ', '');
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
const admin = await Admin.findById(decoded.id);

if (!admin || !admin.is_active) {
return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Admin access required' });
}

req.admin = admin;
next();
} catch (error) {
res.status(403).json({ error: 'Admin access denied' });
}
